                "question": "What is sign extension in binary conversion?",
                "answer": "Sign extension is a necessary step when converting a binary number to a larger bit representation (e.g., 8-bit to 16-bit) while preserving the original number's sign (positive or negative). Improper sign extension is a common source of bugs in low-level code."
