        "content": "<h2>Precision in Time Spans</h2>\n\n<p>A date difference calculator is a highly versatile tool used by project managers, financial analysts, and legal professionals to find the precise span of time between any two dates. Mastering the tool ensures accuracy for contracts, schedules, and billing cycles.</p>\n\n<h3>Step 1: Inputting the Start and End Dates</h3>\n\n<h4>Action: Define the Span</h4>\n\n<p>1.  <strong>Input</strong> the Start Date (e.g., Project Commencement).\n2.  <strong>Input</strong> the End Date (e.g., Today's Date or Contract Expiration).\n3.  <strong>Result:</strong> The tool instantly calculates the difference in years, months, and days.</p>\n\n<h3>Step 2: High-Precision Unit Calculation</h3>\n\n<h4>Action: Granular Metrics</h4>\n\n<p>1.  <strong>Review</strong> the results for total days, total weeks, and total hours elapsed.\n2.  <strong>Use Case:</strong> Total days is often required for calculating interest on loans or the exact duration of a legal waiting period.\n3.  <strong>Crucial Feature:</strong> Ensure the calculator correctly accounts for all leap years that fall within the span of dates, as an incorrect calculation can invalidate financial or legal metrics.</p>\n\n<h3>Step 3: Date Arithmetic (Advanced Use)</h3>\n\n<h4>Action: Adding or Subtracting Time</h4>\n\n<p>1.  <strong>Switch</strong> to the date arithmetic mode.\n2.  <strong>Input:</strong> A start date and a value (e.g., 'Add $180$ days' or 'Subtract $\text{4}$ months').\n3.  <strong>Result:</strong> The calculator instantly provides the target future or past date, simplifying scheduling and deadline setting.  This eliminates the need for manual calendar counting.</p>\n\n<h3>Step 4: Verification</h3>\n\n<h4>Action: Leap Year Check</h4>\n\n<p>Test a date span that crosses a known leap year (e.g., $\text{February 28, 2024}$ to $\text{March 1, 2024}$) to confirm the calculator accurately includes the extra day.</p>",
