                "question": "What is 'color drift' in a codebase?",
                "answer": "Color drift occurs when developers use slightly different versions of the same brand color (e.g., `#007BFF` vs. `#0077FF`) across different components. A centralized generator eliminates this by forcing adherence to a single set of defined color variables."
