        "excerpt": "A detailed look at color palette generator features, including harmony types (monochromatic, complementary), export formats, and accessibility auditing for design systems.",
        "content": "<h2>The Toolkit for Creative and Compliant Design</h2>\n\n<p>A color palette generator is a specialized tool that creates a full spectrum of colors based on a single input color, ensuring that the resulting scheme adheres to established color theory rules. This structured approach to color choice is highly beneficial for both aesthetics and technical integrity.</p>\n\n<h3>I. Key Features</h3>\n\n<h4>A. Color Harmony Modes</h4>\n\n<p><strong>Feature:</strong> The ability to instantly switch between different harmony rules:\n<ul><li><strong>Monochromatic:</strong> Generates shades and tints of one color (calm, cohesive).</li><li><strong>Complementary:</strong> Generates a color that sits directly opposite the base color (high contrast, energetic).</li><li><strong>Analogous:</strong> Generates colors adjacent to the base color (rich, visually comfortable).</li></ul>\n<h4>B. Shades and Tints Generation</h4></p>\n\n<p><strong>Benefit:</strong> Automatically creates the $10$ to $12$ different shades (colors darkened with black) and tints (colors lightened with white) needed for responsive and dark mode design. This eliminates manual color manipulation.</p>\n\n<h4>C. Multiple Export Formats</h4>\n\n<p><strong>Feature:</strong> Provides instant export in $\text{HEX}$ (for web), $\text{RGB}$ (for design), $\text{HSL}$ (for intuitive color manipulation), and $\text{CMYK}$ (for print).</p>\n\n<h3>II. Use Cases in Development</h3>\n\n<ul><li><strong>Design System Creation:</strong> Generating the base color set for an entirely new web application or product line.</li><li><strong>Theming and Customization:</strong> Generating a secondary palette for a user to switch themes (e.g., 'light mode' vs. 'dark mode').</li><li><strong>Status Indicators:</strong> Generating high-contrast colors for alerts and notifications (red for errors, blue for info) that harmonize with the main brand color.</li></ul>\n<h3>III. The Accessibility Benefit</h3>\n\n<p>The tool serves as the first line of defense for accessibility. By ensuring all generated colors can be checked instantly for contrast, it forces the design process to be WCAG-compliant from the very first step, saving significant debugging time later in the $\text{CSS}$ phase. [Image of color wheel showing monochromatic, complementary, and analogous color schemes]</p>",
