                "question": "What is a color gamut?",
                "answer": "Color gamut refers to the complete range of colors that can be accurately reproduced by a specific device or medium (e.g., a printer, a monitor). The range for print ($\text{CMYK}$) is much smaller than for screen ($\text{RGB}$). "
