            {
                "question": "What is the difference between a Will and a Living Will?",
                "answer": "A $\text{Last}$ $\text{Will}$ $\text{and}$ $\text{Testament}$ directs the distribution of assets $\text{after}$ $\text{death}$. A $\text{Living}$ $\text{Will}$ (or $\text{Advance}$ $\text{Directive}$) specifies medical wishes and end-of-life care while the person is still alive but incapacitated."
            },
            {
                "question": "Should digital assets be included in a Will?",
                "answer": "Yes. Digital assets ($\text{cryptocurrency}$, $\text{social}$ $\text{media}$ $\text{passwords}$) should be referenced, though the actual access codes should be stored in a secure, separate document referred to by the Will."
            }
