        "excerpt": "Follow this tutorial to generate, customize, and deploy QR codes for websites, contact sharing, and Wi-Fi networks, ensuring scan reliability and branding.",
        "content": "<h2>Bridging the Digital and Physical World</h2>\n\n<p>A $\text{QR}$ $\text{Code}$ $\text{Generator}$ is a simple tool with powerful applications for marketing, networking, and public information sharing. Mastering the tool ensures the code is visually appealing, reliably scannable, and integrated with necessary tracking metrics.</p>\n\n<h3>Step 1: Define the Content</h3>\n\n<h4>Action: The Target Destination</h4>\n\n<p>1.  <strong>Select</strong> the $\text{QR}$ $\text{Code}$ $\text{Type}$ ($\text{e.g.}$, $\text{Website}$ $\text{URL}$, $\text{Contact}$ $\text{Card}$ ($\text{vCard}$), $\text{Wi}$-$\text{Fi}$ $\text{Login}$).\n2.  <strong>Input</strong> the target data ($\text{e.g.}$, $\text{the}$ $\text{URL}$ $\text{to}$ $\text{the}$ $\text{Doodax}$ $\text{site}$).\n3.  <strong>Crucial Check:</strong> Use a $\text{shortened}$ $\text{URL}$ or a $\text{dynamic}$ $\text{link}$ $\text{tracker}$ to enable tracking and prevent code breakdown.</p>\n\n<h3>Step 2: Customization and Branding</h3>\n\n<h4>Action: Aesthetic Appeal</h4>\n\n<p>1.  <strong>Customize</strong> the $\text{QR}$ $\text{Code}$ $\text{Color}$ $\text{and}$ $\text{Style}$. Use your brand's colors ($\text{Doodax}$ $\text{Blue}$) for the foreground and a pure white background.\n2.  <strong>Integrate</strong> a small logo in the center of the code. <strong>Important:</strong> Ensure the logo does not obscure too much of the code's data pattern, which can lead to scan failure.</p>\n\n<h3>Step 3: Scan Testing</h3>\n\n<h4>Action: Verification</h4>\n\n<p>1.  <strong>Scan</strong> the generated code using $\text{3}$ $\text{to}$ $\text{5}$ $\text{different}$ $\text{devices}$ ($\text{iPhones}$, $\text{Androids}$) and apps.\n2.  <strong>Verify</strong> the scan success rate and the destination link. [Image of a QR code being tested on a mobile device]</p>\n\n<h3>Step 4: Deployment and Tracking</h3>\n\n<h4>Action: Data Collection</h4>\n\n<p>1.  <strong>Deploy</strong> the $\text{QR}$ $\text{Code}$ $\text{on}$ $\text{marketing}$ $\text{materials}$ or $\text{physical}$ $\text{locations}$.\n2.  <strong>Track</strong> the usage using the dynamic $\text{link}$ $\text{tracker}$ to measure the code's $\text{ROI}$ and effectiveness.</p>",
